1. The phone is currently at 60% charged. 2. The phone needs to be fully charged, meaning 100% charged. 3. The difference between the two values is 100% - 60% = 40%. 4. The rate of charging is 1 percentage-point per 3 minutes. 5. Therefore, to charge 40 percentage-points, it will take 40 * 3 = 120 minutes. 6. Convert minutes to hours: 120 minutes / 60 minutes/hour = 2 hours.

So, the answer is 2.
